Z||000002||rockcrawl||11-20-2000||09:53 PM||||I prefer the cloth seats for comfort, but Mr Mikes leather seats are only a few bucks more and they look so sweet! I can't decide!<P>------------------<BR>Jon Lagler<BR>'87 GT<BR>4.9 liter V8 Testarossa Spyder (under construction)<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/rockcrawlsig.jpg"> ||||reg||7
Z||000003||ezsurf||11-20-2000||10:22 PM||||I prefer cloth seats as well.  Leather is nice and looks good, but it is a high maintenance interior.  If you've ever seen cracked or chaffed leather seats, it's usually because somebody didn't take care of it.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Seanh||11-20-2000||10:34 PM||||Leather is easy enough to take care of I think. All you have to do is spray some cleaner on it, and then condition it. I think it is even easier then cloth as far as cleaning goes.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/transsig.gif">  <BR><A HREF="http://www.kdsi.net/~sean" TARGET=_blank>Sean's Fiero Page</A><BR>Sean Heberly<BR>Silver 86 GT 2.8 Auto<BR>Going on to 3.4 in Jan.<BR><I>"If you smoke after sex, you're doing it way to fast".</I>||||reg||1
Z||000005||Oreif||11-21-2000||01:58 AM||||I have leather seats in my daily driver and my Fiero (Mr. Mikes) All you need to do is clean them and I use mink oil to condition them every 3 months. No cracks or chaffes. I have to spry young boys and they haven't ruined the daily driver seats. Cloth seats tend to stain.<BR>But I do know that people like cloth seats. My advise would be to find passenger side seat backs to replace yours. When you get them, before you install them, run them thru the washer. They'll come out looking new! (Ask DXR_DAD he did his this way) As for seat bottoms you need to find a driver and passenger side. (holes are on different sides) Unless you don't car about 2 extra holes on the console side. It would be cheaper than buying the $380.00 seat covers from the Fiero store. <P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||DXR_DAD||11-21-2000||11:59 AM||||Yes my seat covers look NEW! I did just as Oreif said, Pre-soak them with spray-n-wash<BR>Used the pass. side for the drivers, both my <BR>bottoms were in great shape.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>It was one of our good members that gave me a dang good deal on them!!!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P><BR>DXR_DAD||||reg||14
Z||000007||Oreif||11-21-2000||01:57 PM|||| <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000008||rockcrawl||11-21-2000||04:02 PM||||Be careful, be very very careful. I had a pair of perfect stock seat covers that I removed and washed. I hand washed them in the sink with laundry detergent (Tide) and they literally went to pieces. Not sure what made them come apart, the hot water or the soap, but the fabric just disintegrated.<P>------------------<BR>Jon Lagler<BR>'87 GT<BR>4.9 liter V8 Testarossa Spyder (under construction)<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/rockcrawlsig.jpg"> ||||reg||4
Z||000009||ezsurf||11-21-2000||10:24 PM||||I found the cloth seat kits from the Fiero store.  They're $350 a pr in the book I have, but it's a little old, they have probably gone up since then.  For that kind of money, I'll probably go with leather.  Now I've got to figure out how to repair or replace a section of damaged foam. I'm wondering what it would cost to have them re-upholstered.  Has anyone out there checked in to having their seats re-upholstered?||||reg||1
Z||000010||maninblack||11-21-2000||10:58 PM||||i think mr. mike's seats comes with replacement foem||||reg||1
Z||000011||Seanh||11-21-2000||11:30 PM||||I looked into having the seats done in leather before I know about the Forum and Mr. Mikes. They quoted me $700 for the first seat, and then $400 for the second since they would already have the pattern. I was almost going to do it becuase I really love the look and feel of leather, but decided not to, and I am so glad I didnt. I am going to have them do my dash in leather though.||||reg||1
Z||000012||DXR_DAD||11-22-2000||12:55 AM||||Disintegrated Fabric????== fabric had dry-rot<BR>sun damage, or the type of cleaner that was used on them before??<P>I got a price of $900.00 to re-upholster <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><BR>Mr. Mike is a far better deal!! May be the best deal in town. Soon the black toy will have leather <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P><BR>DXR_DAD||||reg||1
Z||000013||WisconsinGT||11-23-2000||02:52 AM||||I was going to get my seats re-upholstered over the summer. By the looks of things in this thread, I would have gotten one hell of a deal. A retired couple where going to do both seats for $200.00. The problem I had, was finding the same material used for the 88GT seats. I/they could not find the stuff. They had every GM interior book. No luck.||||reg||1
Z||000014||horseman||11-24-2000||11:02 PM||||Wasn't there an earlier thread on swapping seats out of a late model firebird or camaro as well? I would think this would be a fine alternative to re-upholstery. Unless you really wanted leather.||||reg||1
Z||000015||johnmac||11-25-2000||07:00 AM||||I just installed Saddleman's Cloth Seat Covers and they are very good for only $199. Got the seats out of Pep Boy - special order.<P>Not show quality but good for a rider car in Hot Florida.<P>Tried to get Cloth seats out of Mr. Mike but he is not interested. Leather is TOO HOT down here in Florida.<P>Johnmac||||reg||1
